WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.237
Time: 4 minutes.

00:00:01.477 --> 00:00:09.712
Use a small set of sections: Purpose; Before you start; Steps; Expected result; Stop and escalate; Owner and review date.

00:00:09.952 --> 00:00:13.771
Start each step with an action and describe what the reader should observe.

00:00:14.011 --> 00:00:18.469
Avoid instructions that depend on tribal knowledge such as ‘do the usual fix.’

00:00:19.159 --> 00:00:24.066
Worked runbook excerpt: ‘Purpose: check the status of a delayed demo export.

00:00:24.306 --> 00:00:30.749
Before you start: confirm this is the DEMO training environment and note the job identifier. 1.

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:33.591
Open the demo export status view. 2.

00:00:33.831 --> 00:00:36.114
Match the job identifier. 3.

00:00:36.354 --> 00:00:40.258
Compare elapsed time with the training threshold of 10 minutes. 4.

00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:42.973
If Complete, use the approved download route.

00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:47.458
If Processing under 10 minutes, wait until the threshold and check once more.

00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:58.045
If Failed or still Processing at 10 minutes, record job ID, status, elapsed time, and the displayed non-sensitive error code; send to the demo support owner.

00:00:58.285 --> 00:01:01.911
Do not rerun a job unless the approved procedure directs it.’

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:10.239
The threshold and route are invented training policy, not Confluence functionality or operational advice for a real system.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:13.316
No real download or escalation occurs here.

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:17.739
Use descriptive link text, heading hierarchy, and concise steps.

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:20.731
Provide text equivalents for meaningful images.

00:01:20.971 --> 00:01:25.729
Screenshots can age quickly; describe the control’s purpose as well as its label.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:35.753
Learner-authored practice (3 minutes): Turn these new fictional notes into a 4–6 step mini-runbook: DEMO queue; check correct job ID; Complete means use

00:01:35.753 --> 00:01:44.964
approved sample download route; Processing under 5 minutes means recheck at 5; Failed or Processing at 5 means stop and contact the Demo Support role;

00:01:44.964 --> 00:01:51.208
include job ID, elapsed time, status, and non-sensitive error code; never rerun without authorization.

00:01:51.448 --> 00:01:53.325
Add a purpose and stop condition.

00:01:53.565 --> 00:01:59.432
This separate exercise uses a 5-minute rule; the main worked case retains its 10-minute rule.

00:01:59.672 --> 00:02:02.616
Compare your writing with the rubric before continuing.

00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:04.394
Now it's your turn.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.343
Which instruction best replaces “Ask Morgan”?

00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:10.698
